    "SQL-SUB-05"
  ],
  "description": "R-SQL-1 SQL-SUB-04, SQL-SUB-05: Does EXISTS demand an unused failing projection, a failing membership predicate whose decisive match comes before the failing row (CLng(t) = 1) or after it (CLng(t) = 2), and do IN memberships with a decisive value before or after the failure raise? Also EXISTS over TOP, DISTINCT, GROUP BY/HAVING and a nested NOT EXISTS. Runs on a fresh copy of r-sql-1-accdb-main opened read-only through ACE DAO; each statement is opened with Database.OpenRecordset as a snapshot unless stated, Fields Name/Type/Size/SourceTable/SourceField are read before the first row, then every row's Field values to EOF (each MoveNext captured), then Close and DBEngine.Errors.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
